Article 10 An overseas non-governmental organization that meets the following conditions may, based on its business scope, activity region and the need to conduct activities, apply to register and establish a representative office within the territory of China:
(1) It is lawfully established outside the territory of China;
(2) It is capable of independently bearing civil liability;
(3) The purpose and business scope stipulated in its articles of association are conducive to the development of public welfare undertakings;
(4) It has existed outside the territory of China for more than two years and has substantively conducted activities; and
(5) Other conditions as provided by laws and administrative regulations.

Article 12 An overseas non-governmental organization shall, within thirty days from the date of consent by the business supervisory unit, apply to the registration management authority for registration of the establishment of a representative office. To apply for registration of the establishment of a representative office, it shall submit the following documents and materials to the registration management authority:
(1) A written application;
(2) Documents and materials certifying compliance with the conditions set forth in Article 10 of this Law;
(3) Identity certificate, resume, and documentary evidence or declaration of no criminal record of the proposed chief representative of the representative office;
(4) Documentary evidence of the domicile of the proposed representative office;
(5) Documentary evidence of the source of funds;
(6) The consent document of the business supervisory unit; and
(7) Other documents and materials as provided by laws and administrative regulations.
The registration management authority, when examining the application for establishment of a representative office of an overseas non-governmental organization, may organize experts to conduct an evaluation as needed.
The registration management authority shall, within sixty days from the date of accepting the application, make a decision on whether to approve the registration or not.

Article 13 For a representative office of an overseas non-governmental organization that is approved for registration, the registration management authority shall issue a registration certificate and make an announcement to the public. The registered items shall include:
(1) Name;
(2) Domicile;
(3) Business scope;
(4) Activity region;
(5) Chief representative; and
(6) Business supervisory unit.
The representative office of an overseas non-governmental organization shall, based on the registration certificate, undergo tax registration according to law, make a seal, open a bank account in a bank within the territory of China, and report a copy of the tax registration certificate, the seal specimen and the bank account to the registration management authority for the record.

Article 15 Under any of the following circumstances, the registration management authority shall cancel the registration of a representative office of an overseas non-governmental organization and announce it to the public:
(1) The overseas non-governmental organization dissolves the representative office;
(2) The overseas non-governmental organization is terminated;
(3) The representative office of the overseas non-governmental organization is lawfully subject to cancellation of registration or revocation of the registration certificate; or
(4) The representative office is terminated due to other reasons.
After the cancellation of registration of a representative office of an overseas non-governmental organization, the overseas non-governmental organization that established the representative office shall properly handle the aftermath matters. A representative office of an overseas non-governmental organization does not have the status of a legal person, and where relevant legal liability is involved, such liability shall be borne by the overseas non-governmental organization.

Article 17 Where an overseas non-governmental organization conducts temporary activities, the Chinese partner unit shall go through the examination and approval formalities in accordance with State regulations and file a record with the registration management authority at the place where it is located fifteen days before the commencement of the temporary activities. The following documents and materials shall be submitted for recordation:
(1) Documents and materials certifying the lawful establishment of the overseas non-governmental organization;
(2) A written agreement between the overseas non-governmental organization and the Chinese partner unit;
(3) Relevant materials such as the name, purpose, region and duration of the temporary activities;
(4) Documents and materials of the project funds and source of funds, and the bank account of the Chinese partner unit;
(5) The document of approval obtained by the Chinese partner unit; and
(6) Other documents and materials as provided by laws and administrative regulations.
Where temporary activities need to be conducted under emergency circumstances such as disaster relief or rescue, the time limit for recordation shall not be subject to the provisions of the preceding paragraph.
The duration of temporary activities shall not exceed one year; where an extension is truly necessary, a new recordation shall be made.
If the registration management authority considers that the recorded temporary activities do not comply with the provisions of Article 5 of this Law, it shall promptly notify the Chinese partner unit to cease the temporary activities.

Article 29 A representative office of an overseas non-governmental organization shall have one chief representative, and may, based on business needs, have one to three representatives.
A person under any of the following circumstances shall not serve as the chief representative or a representative:
(1) Having no civil capacity or having limited civil capacity;
(2) Having a criminal record;
(3) Having served as the chief representative or representative of a representative office that was lawfully subject to cancellation of registration or revocation of the registration certificate, where less than five years have elapsed since the date of such cancellation or revocation; or
(4) Other circumstances as provided by laws and administrative regulations.

Article 41 The public security organs shall be responsible for the registration and annual inspection of representative offices of overseas non-governmental organizations, and the recordation of temporary activities of overseas non-governmental organizations, and shall investigate and punish the illegal acts of overseas non-governmental organizations and their representative offices.
When performing the functions of supervision and administration, if the public security organs discover acts suspected of violating the provisions of this Law, they may take the following measures according to law:
(1) Interview the chief representative and other responsible persons of the representative office of the overseas non-governmental organization;
(2) Enter the domicile and activity venues of the overseas non-governmental organization within the territory of China for on-site inspection;
(3) Inquire about the units and individuals related to the incident under investigation and require them to make explanations on matters related to the incident under investigation;
(4) Consult and make copies of the documents and materials related to the incident under investigation, and seal up the documents and materials that may be transferred, destroyed, concealed or tampered with; and
(5) Seal up or seize the premises, facilities or property suspected of being used in illegal activities.

Article 45 Where a representative office of an overseas non-governmental organization, an overseas non-governmental organization conducting temporary activities, or a Chinese partner unit falls under any of the following circumstances, the public security organ of the people's government at or above the level of a city divided into districts shall give it a warning or order it to cease its activities within a specified time limit; confiscate the illegal property and illegal gains; and if the circumstances are serious, the registration management authority shall revoke the registration certificate or ban the temporary activities:
(1) Failing to undergo alteration registration or file relevant matters for the record as required;
(2) Conducting activities not in accordance with the registered or recorded name, business scope or activity region;
(3) Engaging in or sponsoring for-profit activities, conducting fundraising, or recruiting members in violation of regulations;
(4) Obtaining or using funds in violation of regulations, or failing to open or use bank accounts or conduct accounting as required;
(5) Failing to submit the annual activity plan, or submit or make public the annual work report as required; or
(6) Refusing to accept or failing to accept supervision and inspection as required.
Where a representative office of an overseas non-governmental organization, an overseas non-governmental organization conducting temporary activities, or a Chinese partner unit obtains the registration certificate of a representative office or files temporary activities for the record by illegal means such as providing false materials, or forges, alters, buys, sells, leases or lends the registration certificate or seal, it shall be punished in accordance with the provisions of the preceding paragraph.

Article 46 Under any of the following circumstances, the public security organ of the people's government at or above the level of a city divided into districts shall ban the activities or order the cessation of the illegal acts; confiscate the illegal property and illegal gains; give a warning to the persons directly responsible, and if the circumstances are serious, impose detention of not more than ten days:
(1) Conducting activities in the name of a representative office of an overseas non-governmental organization or an overseas non-governmental organization without registration or recordation;
(2) Conducting activities in the name of a representative office of an overseas non-governmental organization after its registration has been cancelled, its registration certificate has been revoked, or its registration has been canceled;
(3) Conducting activities within the territory of China after the duration of the temporary activities of an overseas non-governmental organization has expired or after the temporary activities have been banned; or
(4) An overseas non-governmental organization, without having registered a representative office or filed temporary activities for the record, entrusts or finances a unit or individual within the territory of China to conduct activities within the territory of China.
Where a unit or individual within the territory of China, knowing that an overseas non-governmental organization has not registered a representative office or its temporary activities have not been filed for the record, cooperates with it, or accepts its entrustment or funding, acts as an agent or acts as an agent in disguised form to conduct activities or to receive or disburse funds for project activities, the unit or individual shall be punished in accordance with the provisions of the preceding paragraph.

Article 47 Where an overseas non-governmental organization or its representative office falls under any of the following circumstances, the registration management authority shall revoke the registration certificate or ban the temporary activities; if the act does not yet constitute a crime, the public security organ of the people's government at or above the level of a city divided into districts shall impose detention of not more than fifteen days on the persons directly responsible:
(1) Inciting resistance to the implementation of laws and regulations;
(2) Illegally obtaining State secrets;
(3) Spreading rumors, defaming, or publishing or disseminating other harmful information, thereby endangering national security or harming national interests;
(4) Engaging in or sponsoring political activities, or illegally engaging in or sponsoring religious activities; or
(5) Otherwise endangering national security, harming national interests or the social public interests.
Where an overseas non-governmental organization or its representative office commits criminal acts such as splitting the State, undermining national unity, or subverting the State power, the registration management authority shall impose penalties in accordance with the provisions of the preceding paragraph, and the persons directly responsible shall be investigated for criminal liability according to law.
